@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam roundCorner 10

title EduCore — Student Academic Portal & Registration Flow

actor "Student" as Student
participant "Vue 3 SPA\n(Inertia.js)" as UI
participant "Student Controller\n& RegistrationService" as Backend
database "PostgreSQL DB" as DB
storage "MinIO Storage" as MinIO

== Student Portal Sign In ==
Student -> UI : Sign in
UI -> Backend : Authenticate session
Backend --> UI : Return role 'student' & student profile
UI -> UI : Redirect to /dashboard
UI -> Backend : GET /dashboard
Backend -> DB : Query student GPA, enrolled courses, attendance rate, invoice balance
Backend --> UI : Render personalized student academic overview

== Course Self-Registration ==
Student -> UI : Navigate to /registration
UI -> Backend : GET /registration
Backend -> DB : Query active semester & open offerings
Backend --> UI : Display available course sections

Student -> UI : Click 'Register' on Section (e.g. CS102-A)
UI -> Backend : POST /registration (section_id)
Backend -> Backend : Validate Registration Window is open
Backend -> Backend : Validate Course Prerequisites
Backend -> Backend : Check Section Capacity (enrolled < max)
Backend -> Backend : Detect Schedule Overlap with other enrolled sections
alt Validation Failure
  Backend --> UI : 422 Unprocessable Entity (Specific rule failure)
  UI --> Student : Display error banner (e.g. Prerequisite CS101 required)
else Validation Passes
  Backend -> DB : Insert enrollments record (status: enrolled)
  Backend -> DB : Increment section enrolled_count
  Backend --> UI : 200 OK (Registration confirmed toast)
end

== Assignment Submission ==
Student -> UI : Open /my-assignments & select task
Student -> UI : Upload PDF file & click 'Submit'
UI -> Backend : POST /assignments/{id}/submissions
Backend -> MinIO : Upload student submission file
Backend -> DB : Insert/update assignment_submissions record (track is_late)
Backend --> UI : Confirm submission recorded toast

== Document Request & QR Verification ==
Student -> UI : Request 'Certificate of Study'
UI -> Backend : POST /my-documents
Backend -> DB : Create document request record
Backend --> UI : Request submitted toast
... Admin Approves and Generates Document ...
Student -> UI : Download issued PDF
actor "Third-Party Verifier" as Verifier
Verifier -> UI : Scans QR code on PDF (/verify/{token})
UI -> Backend : GET /verify/{token}
Backend -> DB : Verify token & document status
Backend --> UI : Display verified official credential badge

@enduml
